WEBVTT

1
00:00:23.032 --> 00:00:30.981
English subtitles by Ddbltrbl

2
00:02:58.226 --> 00:03:01.851
- Are you Inga from Varteig?
- Yes.

3
00:03:02.809 --> 00:03:05.642
We are Birkebeiner.
Is that Haakon Haakonsson?

4
00:03:05.809 --> 00:03:08.226
Yes.

5
00:03:08.392 --> 00:03:12.184
You must join us.
The King commands.

6
00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.892
- Come.
- It's okay, Haakon.

7
00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.892
- Is everything okay with him?
- Yes.

8
00:05:04.059 --> 00:05:10.851
Hey. We are almost there,
then you are completely safe.

9
00:05:12.184 --> 00:05:14.392
That's good.

10
00:05:23.059 --> 00:05:27.684
You live dangerously.
She has children with the King, Torstein.

11
00:05:27.851 --> 00:05:31.934
I'm only maKing sure that
the kid is fine, Skjervald. The kid.

12
00:05:33.351 --> 00:05:37.601
- Now our paths separate, my friend.
- Are you sure of this?

13
00:05:37.767 --> 00:05:40.434
Yes. I know
that the King's son is in good hands.

14
00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:44.184
Can you milk cows?

15
00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:46.934
No, Ylva does that.

16
00:05:48.851 --> 00:05:52.059
If you change your mind,
you know where we are.

17
00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:54.184
- Well home.
- Thanks.

18
00:05:56.726 --> 00:05:59.142
Take care of the kid. The kid.

19
00:06:00.892 --> 00:06:03.601
There is never gonna be enough
farmer in you, Skjervald

20
00:06:50.351 --> 00:06:54.351
- Who is it?
- It's me, Skjervald.

21
00:07:00.726 --> 00:07:03.101
There you are, finally.

22
00:07:05.017 --> 00:07:08.309
Yes, we had to go all the way to Borg.
So...

23
00:07:10.184 --> 00:07:14.642
- You should have been here long ago.
- It took longer than we thought.

24
00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:18.267
This was my last assignment.
I promise, Ylva.

25
00:07:18.434 --> 00:07:22.309
You said you were going to finish the house,
and the storehouse should be done.

26
00:07:22.476 --> 00:07:25.767
I know.
It will be completed.

27
00:07:25.934 --> 00:07:28.309
For next winter?

28
00:07:28.476 --> 00:07:30.934
This summer.

29
00:07:31.101 --> 00:07:34.226
This summer?
You promise?

30
00:07:36.267 --> 00:07:39.017
I promise, Ylva.

31
00:07:40.184 --> 00:07:46.642
Not more with Birkebeiner. I'll
just be here with you and Eirik.

32
00:07:50.976 --> 00:07:53.267
I promise.

33
00:07:59.642 --> 00:08:02.101
Is he sleeping?

34
00:08:06.809 --> 00:08:09.392
No, you do not sleep.

35
00:08:13.684 --> 00:08:15.226
Look here.

36
00:08:17.851 --> 00:08:19.767
Look there.

37
00:08:21.309 --> 00:08:23.476
And there.

38
00:08:26.642 --> 00:08:28.142
Hey.

39
00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:32.184
Oh. No.

40
00:08:33.434 --> 00:08:35.351
Come.

41
00:09:40.267 --> 00:09:44.642
It's only you who can
get close to him, so you must do it.

42
00:09:44.809 --> 00:09:48.601
For God's sake, Gisle,
Haakon is my stepson.

43
00:09:48.726 --> 00:09:51.601
He is King, Margrete.

44
00:09:51.767 --> 00:09:55.517
He is so young that he does not understand
that the Birkebeiner's is the past.

45
00:09:55.684 --> 00:09:59.892
Baglers win the war,
and I will exploit that.

46
00:10:04.517 --> 00:10:08.892
You meet him alone.
He trusts you. It's fine.

47
00:10:14.392 --> 00:10:18.601
Think if something... Think about if
it doesn't go as we planned?

48
00:10:19.642 --> 00:10:23.976
Of course it will go as planned. 
Everyone will believe it is Inge.

49
00:10:24.142 --> 00:10:27.976
When he stands first in line to the throne,
no one will suspect us.

50
00:10:33.601 --> 00:10:34.934
Here.

51
00:10:37.767 --> 00:10:40.142
Soon you will be queen again.

52
00:11:16.326 --> 00:11:17.701
Mother?

53
00:11:21.201 --> 00:11:23.326
You can not do it.

54
00:11:24.701 --> 00:11:25.951
What?

55
00:11:26.117 --> 00:11:28.201
I heard what he said.

56
00:11:33.409 --> 00:11:36.534
You've never heard anything.

57
00:11:37.742 --> 00:11:41.409
Do you understand what I'm saying?
Nothing.

58
00:11:44.201 --> 00:11:46.701
Can you promise me that?

59
00:11:48.409 --> 00:11:52.326
If this gets out, -

60
00:11:52.492 --> 00:11:54.451
- We die.

61
00:11:57.326 --> 00:12:01.326
My beloved, beloved daughter.
Forgive me. Forgive me.

62
00:12:04.201 --> 00:12:08.909
I have to go back to Sweden,
but when we meet again -

63
00:12:09.076 --> 00:12:14.034
- I stand as bride in the Nidaros Cathedral
and become queen again.

64
00:12:14.201 --> 00:12:18.992
And you...
You shall be my... princess.

65
00:12:21.367 --> 00:12:26.284
I know it's a big task.
You have a long journey ahead of you.

66
00:12:26.451 --> 00:12:31.284
But Sweden is important and you are the
only one who can win their trust.

67
00:12:32.326 --> 00:12:38.201
You have to get them to break with the church
and support us in the fight against the Baglers.

68
00:12:42.201 --> 00:12:46.117
My father is watching us, Margrete.
Let's make him proud.

69
00:12:54.826 --> 00:12:56.992
Cheers, my friend.

70
00:12:59.201 --> 00:13:01.242
For Norway.

71
00:13:04.201 --> 00:13:07.367
I want to thank you, Margaret.

72
00:13:07.534 --> 00:13:11.992
You stood faithfully by my father's side
every day of his life.

73
00:13:14.201 --> 00:13:17.409
I have seen your sorrow
since father died, -

74
00:13:17.576 --> 00:13:21.492
- And I know you miss him
as much as I do.

75
00:13:31.076 --> 00:13:34.034
I have lost all my loved ones.

76
00:13:35.742 --> 00:13:38.909
I have only you and Christina again.

77
00:13:42.367 --> 00:13:45.076
To all your love. Toast.

78
00:14:05.867 --> 00:14:08.034
Goodbye, my son.

79
00:14:09.701 --> 00:14:11.992
Goodbye, Margrete.

80
00:14:34.326 --> 00:14:36.409
Get... get me Inge Baardsson!

81
00:14:42.242 --> 00:14:44.826
Gisle, where is Inge?

82
00:14:51.034 --> 00:14:52.784
Inge!

83
00:14:53.909 --> 00:14:58.284
In Borg I shared bed with a woman,
Inga from Varteig.

84
00:14:58.451 --> 00:15:02.492
She gave birth to my son, Haakon Haakonsson.
He will inherit the throne.

85
00:15:02.659 --> 00:15:06.659
Birkebeiners in Eastern Norway
leads him north.

86
00:15:06.826 --> 00:15:09.326
Meet them with an army
in the Oesterdalen!

87
00:15:56.834 --> 00:15:59.751
We have a traitor among us.

88
00:16:00.917 --> 00:16:04.209
Here in this room.

89
00:16:04.376 --> 00:16:08.376
Widow Queen Margrete poisoned
King, but she was not alone.

90
00:16:08.542 --> 00:16:11.792
She was a pawn in a game.

91
00:16:11.959 --> 00:16:15.334
The traitor thinks
that Rome has won the battle for Norway.

92
00:16:15.501 --> 00:16:21.001
That he will not have to pay for his
sins, but believe me, Birkebeiner...

93
00:16:21.959 --> 00:16:26.751
I'll find him. No one get out.
The gate is locked.

94
00:16:26.917 --> 00:16:30.334
So we send an army southward
to find the King's son.

95
00:16:30.501 --> 00:16:33.917
No one leaves the royal estate
before the traitor is taken.

96
00:16:44.709 --> 00:16:47.876
My brother is under strong pressure.

97
00:16:49.542 --> 00:16:52.959
If not he sees
an opportunity to become King himself.

98
00:16:53.126 --> 00:16:54.209
What do you mean?

99
00:16:54.376 --> 00:16:57.251
Inge is quick to accuse us,
the King's closest men, -

100
00:16:57.417 --> 00:17:03.876
- And his kinsman, his own brother.
Gisle and Inge are not royal sons.

101
00:17:04.042 --> 00:17:09.084
But if Sverres heritage dies with Haakon
Haakonsson, one of them will inherit the throne.

102
00:17:09.251 --> 00:17:13.209
And Inge is the oldest. It is Inge
standing first in line.

103
00:17:13.376 --> 00:17:18.417
Inge Baardsson is the one who has the most
to gain from the King's death.

104
00:17:18.584 --> 00:17:21.834
Then he will accuse us
faithful Birkebeiner, -

105
00:17:22.001 --> 00:17:25.626
- Which has served the Norwegian King's
since before he was born.

106
00:17:25.792 --> 00:17:29.792
Not Inge, but Haakon Haakonsson is the
rightful heir to the throne of Norway, -

107
00:17:29.959 --> 00:17:32.834
- And the boy's life is in danger.
If the King's son dies -

108
00:17:33.001 --> 00:17:38.001
- We become a puppet state under
Denmark. The Pope will rule us.

109
00:17:38.167 --> 00:17:42.584
So... what will you do, Gisle?

110
00:17:46.084 --> 00:17:49.417
Anyone trying to get out,
should be locked up. Ravn.

111
00:17:50.709 --> 00:17:53.501
Collect your men
and bring the King's son here.

112
00:18:41.334 --> 00:18:44.626
A Birkebeiner from Nidaros.

113
00:19:05.801 --> 00:19:07.884
It is from Earl Gisle.

114
00:19:24.009 --> 00:19:27.801
We have just received news
from Nidaros.

115
00:19:29.051 --> 00:19:31.051
King Haakon is dead.

116
00:19:33.134 --> 00:19:37.217
Birkebeiners have lost
its unifying force.

117
00:19:37.801 --> 00:19:41.967
The King's time is over.
But the church will always remain.

118
00:19:43.676 --> 00:19:46.092
When a man falls,
another will take his place.

119
00:19:46.259 --> 00:19:49.176
And he accountable only to God.

120
00:19:51.592 --> 00:19:56.051
We reign Eastern Norway.
Western Norway's next.

121
00:19:57.551 --> 00:20:01.426
Soon the church have power
throughout the Kingdom of Norway.

122
00:20:02.842 --> 00:20:05.342
But one thing remains.

123
00:20:13.426 --> 00:20:17.051
King Haakon
has left a son.

124
00:20:19.717 --> 00:20:23.176
Today an innocent boy.

125
00:20:23.342 --> 00:20:25.259
Tomorrow...

126
00:20:25.426 --> 00:20:28.217
Our most powerful enemy.

127
00:20:28.384 --> 00:20:32.176
The boy is kept hidden
on a farm here in our area.

128
00:20:32.342 --> 00:20:36.509
Whoever finds the King's son shall
live in prosperity the rest of his life.

129
00:20:37.592 --> 00:20:40.509
And do not be merciful
in your search for the child, -

130
00:20:40.676 --> 00:20:45.176
- Thy Lord is forever merciful,
but he also requires sacrifice.

131
00:20:45.342 --> 00:20:48.592
Let law and order depart on your way.

132
00:20:50.176 --> 00:20:52.634
And bring me the boy's head.

133
00:21:24.176 --> 00:21:26.967
So, so, Eirik, it's okay.

134
00:21:29.592 --> 00:21:31.551
Shh.

135
00:22:45.301 --> 00:22:48.176
It's a tough wife you have.

136
00:22:48.342 --> 00:22:50.217
Very strong.

137
00:22:52.842 --> 00:22:54.717
What have you done with Ylva?

138
00:22:54.884 --> 00:22:58.884
Everything is good. All is well.

139
00:23:01.676 --> 00:23:03.967
Ylva? Ylva!

140
00:23:04.301 --> 00:23:06.467
Skjervald, we are here.

141
00:23:09.551 --> 00:23:14.801
There is a boy of royal blood.
Where is the boy hidden?

142
00:23:18.009 --> 00:23:21.217
I don't know what you're talking about.

143
00:23:23.467 --> 00:23:26.009
Are you really so indifferent
with your family -

144
00:23:26.176 --> 00:23:29.717
- You will sacrifice
their lives for a dead King?

145
00:23:39.342 --> 00:23:40.842
Get it over with.

146
00:23:41.009 --> 00:23:44.134
- Skjervald!
- No, wait! Wait!

147
00:23:48.217 --> 00:23:51.551
The King's son is in Borg.

148
00:23:51.717 --> 00:23:54.009
He was Borg.

149
00:23:55.926 --> 00:23:59.509
You and Thorstein led him away.
I saw you.

150
00:24:03.301 --> 00:24:07.717
Just tell where the boy is,
then he lets Ylva and your son live.

151
00:24:11.051 --> 00:24:13.384
The King is dead, Skjervald.

152
00:24:14.926 --> 00:24:17.509
Tell where the boy is.

153
00:24:22.301 --> 00:24:25.592
Okay, I'll show the way.
I will join you.

154
00:24:26.676 --> 00:24:29.342
In which direction?

155
00:24:30.134 --> 00:24:32.092
North.

156
00:24:32.259 --> 00:24:34.134
Where?

157
00:24:36.842 --> 00:24:40.009
Where river runs into Mjoesa.

158
00:24:40.176 --> 00:24:43.926
- I know where. I will show you the way.
- Damn traitor.

159
00:24:53.884 --> 00:24:56.801
You broke right away.

160
00:24:56.967 --> 00:24:59.926
There is no fight in you.

161
00:25:00.092 --> 00:25:02.801
Your wife did not say a word.

162
00:25:07.509 --> 00:25:11.634
No matter what we did to her.

163
00:25:17.634 --> 00:25:19.676
No!

164
00:26:02.551 --> 00:26:04.259
Get him out.

165
00:26:36.967 --> 00:26:38.426
After him!

166
00:26:58.101 --> 00:27:00.101
Where is the boy?

167
00:27:31.017 --> 00:27:33.184
Is it for me?

168
00:27:33.351 --> 00:27:36.684
- Thanks.
- Thanks.

169
00:27:46.351 --> 00:27:50.684
You, Haakon Haakonsson,
now you have to sleep a little.

170
00:28:03.892 --> 00:28:06.642
Are you hungry?

171
00:28:06.809 --> 00:28:08.767
No thanks.

172
00:28:09.726 --> 00:28:11.559
Safe?

173
00:28:12.892 --> 00:28:15.892
I can take one.

174
00:28:16.101 --> 00:28:20.684
You know, if you give me a little bit,
 I eat the whole dish.

175
00:28:35.476 --> 00:28:38.309
- Can I try it?
- Yes, yes.

176
00:28:39.434 --> 00:28:44.101
No, no, no.
You have to keep it that way.

177
00:28:44.226 --> 00:28:47.392
If a Bagle come towards you,
do this.

178
00:28:49.101 --> 00:28:50.684
Okay.

179
00:28:51.267 --> 00:28:54.517
That's it. Good. Like that.
Bulk down the legs.

180
00:28:54.809 --> 00:28:56.976
Down in the legs.

181
00:29:00.309 --> 00:29:04.101
When your father was young, Egil,
he was the baddest warrior.

182
00:29:05.226 --> 00:29:08.809
- Was he a Birkebeiner?
- Have you not told about it?

183
00:29:11.642 --> 00:29:15.642
Glory to the Birkebeiners
and all that you are fighting for.

184
00:29:17.726 --> 00:29:21.517
But being a farmer
and putting food on the table, -

185
00:29:21.684 --> 00:29:24.267
- It is the grandest
thing a man can do.

186
00:29:24.434 --> 00:29:28.851
Just wait. 
We'll make a Birkebeiner of your boy.

187
00:29:50.817 --> 00:29:53.317
Trym, you can go.

188
00:30:03.859 --> 00:30:08.234
Your father has experienced a lot of pain,
Egil. Many of us have.

189
00:30:08.401 --> 00:30:11.984
But we are free.
So keep your eyes open.

190
00:30:12.151 --> 00:30:14.442
I will.

191
00:30:16.442 --> 00:30:18.817
- And ears.
- Yes.

192
00:30:38.817 --> 00:30:42.484
Someone's coming!
Torstein, someone comes.

193
00:30:46.276 --> 00:30:47.651
- Where?
- There.

194
00:30:51.067 --> 00:30:53.442
Gate!

195
00:30:53.609 --> 00:30:55.651
Stay!

196
00:31:02.192 --> 00:31:04.776
It's Baglers.
Get the King's son out of here!

197
00:31:04.942 --> 00:31:07.776
Get people ready and bring Erlend. Now!

198
00:31:13.192 --> 00:31:17.192
Skjervald. What's happened?
What's happened?

199
00:31:18.901 --> 00:31:21.859
- Ylva.
- Come.

200
00:31:31.442 --> 00:31:34.276
- The horse is ready. Get more food.
- Yes.

201
00:31:34.442 --> 00:31:36.817
Get the boy away from here.

202
00:31:36.984 --> 00:31:40.776
We together to
Auduns farm and we take Oesterdalen.

203
00:31:40.942 --> 00:31:43.651
You go. I am staying here.

204
00:31:48.859 --> 00:31:52.109
Erlend, we are ready to go.

205
00:31:52.276 --> 00:31:54.609
Where did you see the Baglers?

206
00:31:54.776 --> 00:31:57.942
- They can be here anytime.
- Where?

207
00:31:58.109 --> 00:32:00.817
- They attacked my farm.
- How many?

208
00:32:00.984 --> 00:32:02.776
Around 12 men.

209
00:32:04.026 --> 00:32:05.401
Only 12?

210
00:32:05.526 --> 00:32:08.609
They brought with them one of ours.
A Birkebeiner.

211
00:32:08.776 --> 00:32:12.442
Staale. Yes, there could be more.

212
00:32:12.609 --> 00:32:17.067
We must get Haakon away from here before it's
too late. I'll stay and delay the Baglers.

213
00:32:17.234 --> 00:32:20.651
The boy is safe.
We have guards and scouts everywhere.

214
00:32:20.817 --> 00:32:23.942
No, we go north now.

215
00:32:24.109 --> 00:32:26.317
The boy stays.

216
00:32:26.484 --> 00:32:28.984
It is the King's order.

217
00:32:30.776 --> 00:32:32.609
The King is dead.

218
00:32:46.151 --> 00:32:49.151
The Baglers know that Haakon is here.

219
00:32:53.234 --> 00:32:55.984
How the hell do they know that?

220
00:33:00.692 --> 00:33:03.151
I told them that.

221
00:33:08.692 --> 00:33:13.192
We go, but first you will see -

222
00:33:13.401 --> 00:33:16.942
- What we do with the
who betrays our right.

223
00:33:19.901 --> 00:33:21.484
Skjervald.

224
00:33:29.401 --> 00:33:31.026
Brethren

225
00:33:33.317 --> 00:33:37.401
Our rights and our blood
is in all times met with resistance.

226
00:33:39.234 --> 00:33:43.859
Shoulder to shoulder, we have
fought and bled for each other.

227
00:33:45.276 --> 00:33:47.692
- Gard?
- But what happened?

228
00:33:47.859 --> 00:33:51.901
- Torstein, we go now.
- Someone has betrayed us.

229
00:33:53.526 --> 00:33:57.484
We... who drink side by side.

230
00:33:59.651 --> 00:34:02.859
Skjervald, you have betrayed the King.

231
00:34:03.026 --> 00:34:04.609
Wait!

232
00:34:05.651 --> 00:34:11.401
Skjervald is one of us.
He has always been.

233
00:34:15.317 --> 00:34:17.942
Show that you are faithful to the King.

234
00:34:20.692 --> 00:34:23.651
Do it, Torstein,
and get the King's son out of here.

235
00:34:28.651 --> 00:34:31.401
No.

236
00:34:31.526 --> 00:34:35.109
I... I will not.

237
00:34:38.067 --> 00:34:40.567
Then you become the next.

238
00:34:41.942 --> 00:34:45.901
Here we cut down those who betray us.

239
00:34:47.192 --> 00:34:52.401
You will see what awaits
those who betray us!

240
00:34:52.526 --> 00:34:56.276
We will defend our right!

241
00:34:59.192 --> 00:35:02.692
- Baglers!
- Attack!

242
00:35:14.651 --> 00:35:17.026
Run to the sled and get out of here.

243
00:35:32.984 --> 00:35:34.776
No!

244
00:35:45.567 --> 00:35:47.234
Run!

245
00:35:48.817 --> 00:35:50.984
Take the fastest route to the Eastern Valleys.
I'll take the kid.

246
00:35:51.151 --> 00:35:52.734
- No!
- Betrayer!

247
00:35:55.734 --> 00:35:59.984
Inga, listen! We will take care of him.

248
00:36:00.151 --> 00:36:03.651
You have my word.
Come on. Get out!

249
00:36:09.401 --> 00:36:11.192
Torstein!

250
00:36:42.692 --> 00:36:44.776
To the horses!

251
00:36:53.651 --> 00:36:58.234
Baglers! Come on! Come on!
Come on! Come on!

252
00:37:07.067 --> 00:37:10.901
Come on. In here. Here.

253
00:37:41.634 --> 00:37:44.134
Give them a choice.

254
00:37:44.301 --> 00:37:48.717
Fight alongside us or die.

255
00:37:49.426 --> 00:37:54.592
Your word is my law, my lord.

256
00:38:00.801 --> 00:38:06.967
Those of you who will live must
fight for church. The choice is yours.

257
00:38:42.384 --> 00:38:47.509
- Skjervald! We have shaken them off.
- Shh. He is asleep.

258
00:38:47.676 --> 00:38:50.134
- He sleeps.
- Is he sleeping?

259
00:38:50.342 --> 00:38:53.467
Help me
to get him up on my back.

260
00:39:02.592 --> 00:39:04.801
Good. Come.

261
00:39:25.467 --> 00:39:27.051
Gisle.

262
00:39:29.092 --> 00:39:30.926
Get me out of here.

263
00:39:34.801 --> 00:39:37.259
You can not do this alone.

264
00:39:37.426 --> 00:39:39.467
Not without me.

265
00:39:40.592 --> 00:39:44.259
It seems like you've been 
wrong about me, Inge.

266
00:39:46.051 --> 00:39:48.176
A long time.

267
00:39:50.634 --> 00:39:54.551
I know it was not you 
who killed the King.

268
00:39:54.717 --> 00:39:57.634
Because it was I
who did it.

269
00:39:57.801 --> 00:40:00.384
You should know...

270
00:40:02.717 --> 00:40:05.551
That King Sverre's line, -

271
00:40:06.634 --> 00:40:09.051
- It ends here.

272
00:40:16.426 --> 00:40:19.134
Forgive me, brother.

273
00:40:19.301 --> 00:40:21.801
I have never let you prove yourself.

274
00:40:22.926 --> 00:40:26.134
Everything you wanted to do
I have stood in the way of, -

275
00:40:26.301 --> 00:40:28.592
- But now it's your turn.

276
00:40:28.801 --> 00:40:31.801
Show what goodness
which lies within you.

277
00:40:35.926 --> 00:40:38.259
Save the King's son.

278
00:40:54.676 --> 00:40:58.467
You have never known me, brother.

279
00:41:00.092 --> 00:41:02.801
You do not know who I am.

280
00:41:44.451 --> 00:41:47.284
- Do you sleep here, too?
- No.

281
00:41:57.076 --> 00:41:58.742
Christina?

282
00:42:00.326 --> 00:42:03.826
Has there been anyone 
here at night lately?

283
00:42:08.742 --> 00:42:09.867
You?

284
00:42:12.242 --> 00:42:14.076
Christina.

285
00:42:15.701 --> 00:42:17.784
I saw no one.

286
00:42:38.409 --> 00:42:40.576
Christina?

287
00:42:42.451 --> 00:42:46.201
I realize
that this is very difficult.

288
00:42:49.201 --> 00:42:51.826
But now you have to trust me.

289
00:42:53.576 --> 00:42:56.659
You do not speak with anyone,
do nothing.

290
00:42:57.701 --> 00:43:01.617
I am the only one who can protect
you now. Do you understand?

291
00:43:01.784 --> 00:43:03.201
Yes.

292
00:43:03.867 --> 00:43:06.201
Yes.

293
00:43:23.409 --> 00:43:25.617
Torstein?

294
00:43:26.409 --> 00:43:29.076
How is he?

295
00:43:35.867 --> 00:43:40.367
He's very good.
Hi! Hello, good day.

296
00:43:40.784 --> 00:43:44.742
Hello, hello, hello. Hello.

297
00:43:47.076 --> 00:43:48.826
Shall we move on?

298
00:43:48.992 --> 00:43:51.409
We have to get him to 
Auduns farm before dark.

299
00:44:20.034 --> 00:44:22.909
It's okay.
It's okay, Egil.

300
00:44:49.784 --> 00:44:51.992
- Is there something wrong with him?
- What?

301
00:44:52.201 --> 00:44:55.617
He's crying.
He's going to freeze to death!

302
00:44:57.659 --> 00:45:00.492
It is going well. Look here.

303
00:45:03.742 --> 00:45:08.076
- We have to find shelter!
- There are some buildings there.

304
00:45:34.701 --> 00:45:37.367
Torstein!

305
00:45:37.534 --> 00:45:39.492
Look!

306
00:46:07.951 --> 00:46:10.909
Come on. He's freezing.

307
00:46:12.076 --> 00:46:16.492
Take him out. We are safe here
while the storm last.

308
00:46:19.451 --> 00:46:21.201
Here.

309
00:46:28.076 --> 00:46:30.576
Look here. Look.

310
00:46:32.284 --> 00:46:34.826
His hands are warm.

311
00:46:34.992 --> 00:46:37.367
It's royal blood.

312
00:46:39.201 --> 00:46:41.534
He's a tough bastard.

313
00:46:41.701 --> 00:46:43.409
Yes.

314
00:46:45.117 --> 00:46:46.992
Do we have any food?

315
00:46:47.201 --> 00:46:49.201
No.

316
00:46:50.367 --> 00:46:53.492
So, so, so. So, so, so...

317
00:47:12.659 --> 00:47:15.326
Haakon, Haakon. Look here. Look.

318
00:47:15.492 --> 00:47:17.367
Look. Look.

319
00:47:20.492 --> 00:47:22.326
Look here.

320
00:47:23.076 --> 00:47:25.951
Look. Look.

321
00:47:27.451 --> 00:47:29.701
Look here. Look, Haakon. Look.

322
00:47:32.742 --> 00:47:34.992
Look at that. Look.

323
00:47:37.284 --> 00:47:43.201
Gallop gallop galloping.
Once upon a time there was a little...

324
00:47:43.992 --> 00:47:46.076
King horse.

325
00:47:46.242 --> 00:47:51.909
No, an ordinary horse.
And the horse... wanted to be King.

326
00:47:53.409 --> 00:47:59.201
Haakon. But to become King he had
to ride through a mountain of fire.

327
00:48:00.242 --> 00:48:03.826
But it was too hot
so every timer he stopped.

328
00:48:05.534 --> 00:48:07.492
But one day...

329
00:48:08.451 --> 00:48:11.326
He found the fire within himself.

330
00:48:11.492 --> 00:48:17.201
And then he rode through the fire. Ouch.

331
00:48:18.867 --> 00:48:24.409
And therefore he has
come all the way here to you.

332
00:48:24.576 --> 00:48:25.992
Yes.

333
00:48:31.742 --> 00:48:33.367
King's horse.

334
00:48:35.826 --> 00:48:38.117
<i>Oh look...</i>

335
00:48:40.451 --> 00:48:44.492
Look here. Haakon.
Here you have some water.

336
00:48:44.909 --> 00:48:46.701
<i>Look.</i>

337
00:48:47.576 --> 00:48:50.242
Do you want some water?

338
00:48:50.992 --> 00:48:53.034
<i>Look.</i>

339
00:49:05.826 --> 00:49:07.867
Right. Good.

340
00:49:11.742 --> 00:49:15.076
Can I get the horse? Look.

341
00:50:02.651 --> 00:50:04.734
Torstein.

342
00:50:04.901 --> 00:50:07.609
Torstein, I have to go.

343
00:50:07.776 --> 00:50:09.651
What?

344
00:50:09.817 --> 00:50:13.234
It's not far to Auduns farm.
He will help you further.

345
00:50:14.609 --> 00:50:19.401
Baglers will not expect me in the storm.
They do not realize until it's too late.

346
00:50:19.567 --> 00:50:24.401
Will you leave me with the King's son
in the middle of the mountains, in a snowstorm?

347
00:50:26.109 --> 00:50:30.484
- I do not know up from down with the boy.
- Torstein, I must do this.

348
00:50:32.817 --> 00:50:36.109
We do this together, dammit!

349
00:50:36.276 --> 00:50:40.484
Norway's future lies there,
and it is your fault that we're here.

350
00:50:40.651 --> 00:50:43.192
- My fault?
- Yes, it is.

351
00:50:47.067 --> 00:50:53.401
Ylva said nothing.
Nothing. Do you understand that?

352
00:50:53.526 --> 00:50:57.151
Do you understand
how strong she must have been?

353
00:50:57.317 --> 00:51:00.901
She fought to the last.
And what did I do?

354
00:51:06.692 --> 00:51:09.401
Skjervald.

355
00:51:09.567 --> 00:51:12.192
I have to kill him.

356
00:51:15.401 --> 00:51:20.817
You'll have your revenge, Skjervald.
It is your right, and it is your duty.

357
00:51:22.609 --> 00:51:26.984
But it does not help the
defenseless little boy there.

358
00:51:32.984 --> 00:51:36.567
This is the only thing that proves -

359
00:51:36.734 --> 00:51:39.901
- that Haakon is our next King.

360
00:51:43.984 --> 00:51:46.151
And now I give it to you.

361
00:51:48.567 --> 00:51:50.067
Here.

362
00:51:54.401 --> 00:51:59.317
We will all die, Skjervald.
But our legacy lives on.

363
00:52:20.701 --> 00:52:25.867
There are rumors that King Haakon
has a son.

364
00:52:26.576 --> 00:52:29.284
The rumors are true.

365
00:52:31.409 --> 00:52:37.034
We have done everything to get
the heir to Nidaros.

366
00:52:39.826 --> 00:52:42.409
But...

367
00:52:43.617 --> 00:52:47.534
Winter can be ruthless.
We all know that.

368
00:52:48.534 --> 00:52:52.492
And it hurts me
having to tell -

369
00:52:53.784 --> 00:52:56.992
- That the boy died
in a storm in the mountains.

370
00:52:58.742 --> 00:53:01.284
The King's son is dead.

371
00:53:02.701 --> 00:53:05.451
It is with great humility-

372
00:53:06.576 --> 00:53:12.034
- That I have accepted the appointment
to become the new King of Norway.

373
00:53:15.742 --> 00:53:18.451
In order to ensure the country an heir -

374
00:53:18.617 --> 00:53:22.409
- I will marry
with King Sverre's daughter Christina.

375
00:53:29.492 --> 00:53:33.159
Together we will make
peace in our country.

376
00:53:34.784 --> 00:53:38.117
Those who once were our enemies,
will be our friends.

377
00:53:38.284 --> 00:53:43.909
Swords will be laid down, and the battle
with the church will be buried for good.

378
00:53:45.867 --> 00:53:48.701
You will see a new Norway.

379
00:54:16.951 --> 00:54:20.159
Torstein. Torstein.
The storm has subsided.

380
00:54:21.701 --> 00:54:23.617
Take Haakon.

381
00:54:50.076 --> 00:54:54.159
Torstein! Torstein! They are here.

382
00:55:00.951 --> 00:55:02.701
They've seen us.

383
00:55:02.826 --> 00:55:05.284
So, so, so, so.

384
00:55:06.284 --> 00:55:08.201
Come. You go first.

385
00:55:11.867 --> 00:55:13.534
Come!

386
00:57:03.642 --> 00:57:05.517
Take them, dammit!

387
00:57:15.309 --> 00:57:17.559
Skjervald! Watch out!

388
00:57:25.892 --> 00:57:30.309
- Torstein! Are you okay?
- He's alive! So. Come!

389
00:57:30.601 --> 00:57:32.517
Continue!

390
00:57:36.517 --> 00:57:38.892
There is more of them.

391
00:57:39.101 --> 00:57:41.601
Continue! I'll take them!

392
00:58:00.184 --> 00:58:02.017
No!

393
00:58:04.476 --> 00:58:05.684
No.

394
00:58:16.684 --> 00:58:18.809
Torstein!

395
00:58:19.142 --> 00:58:21.267
Torstein!

396
00:58:47.017 --> 00:58:50.267
- Torstein! Torstein! Are you okay?
- No, dammit!

397
00:58:50.434 --> 00:58:53.559
- Give me the kid.
- No, we must continue!

398
00:58:56.684 --> 00:58:58.892
Come. Come on!

399
00:59:20.567 --> 00:59:22.567
Inga!

400
00:59:23.609 --> 00:59:27.942
Welcome to the farm.
Did you find a child?

401
00:59:29.192 --> 00:59:32.442
Oh, my boy! You're alive!

402
00:59:34.026 --> 00:59:36.859
My baby.

403
00:59:37.026 --> 00:59:39.276
Thanks, Torstein.

404
00:59:39.984 --> 00:59:43.651
- So, so. Mommy's here.
- Torstein!

405
00:59:45.192 --> 00:59:48.817
Torstein! Take him inside.
We must get out the arrow.

406
00:59:53.859 --> 00:59:55.026
Ready?

407
00:59:59.109 --> 01:00:02.442
- Calm. Stay calm.
- Get that bottle there.

408
01:00:05.026 --> 01:00:08.901
No, not that. There is fish oil.
The next one.

409
01:00:09.067 --> 01:00:13.192
Take it easy.
This I have done before. On reindeer.

410
01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:15.484
Stay here. Stay. Stay.

411
01:00:21.276 --> 01:00:23.984
That... it helps nothing.

412
01:00:27.942 --> 01:00:32.734
- If I die, I will kill you.
- Yes, yes, yes.

413
01:00:36.026 --> 01:00:38.234
Frikk, hold him down.

414
01:00:39.776 --> 01:00:42.526
- Are you ready?
- No!

415
01:00:58.776 --> 01:01:00.526
Calm now.

416
01:01:15.859 --> 01:01:17.901
- I'll take it.
- Never.

417
01:01:18.067 --> 01:01:21.151
Remember what happened last time.

418
01:01:26.317 --> 01:01:30.067
We have to gather an army, Audun.
We must get Haakon to Nidaros.

419
01:01:31.234 --> 01:01:35.567
An army? Can not you go
and collect an army, Frikk?

420
01:01:38.067 --> 01:01:41.151
The only thing you'll find here
are ordinary people.

421
01:01:41.317 --> 01:01:46.192
Hunters, farmers, tenant farmers
and a fair maiden or two.

422
01:01:46.401 --> 01:01:50.692
We need warriors, Audun.
Send for the King's men.

423
01:01:52.651 --> 01:01:55.317
The King, yes.

424
01:01:55.484 --> 01:01:58.067
Yes, he didn't lasted long.

425
01:01:58.234 --> 01:02:02.984
Fenrir is loose. Rumors says
that Nidaros is completely out of control.

426
01:02:03.151 --> 01:02:09.192
No one knows who has the power. 
It could be us. It could be the Baglers.

427
01:02:16.651 --> 01:02:19.734
Right. Let's get him into the sauna.

428
01:02:50.817 --> 01:02:54.067
I know how you feel.

429
01:02:54.234 --> 01:02:57.401
I have also lost my family.

430
01:03:14.484 --> 01:03:16.234
Egil?

431
01:03:18.776 --> 01:03:21.776
- Can I trust you?
- Yes.

432
01:03:23.192 --> 01:03:25.484
- Go up the mountain there.
- Up there?

433
01:03:25.651 --> 01:03:29.026
Yes. And then you find
a place with great views south.

434
01:03:29.192 --> 01:03:31.484
- It's okay.
- Then you pay attention all the time.

435
01:03:31.651 --> 01:03:35.151
Do not sleep on duty. Do not be afraid.
Do you understand that?

436
01:03:35.317 --> 01:03:39.984
If you see someone, you find the
quickest way back here.

437
01:03:51.317 --> 01:03:56.401
Lord, heal his wound,
and free him from all suffering.

438
01:03:57.692 --> 01:04:01.526
Give him health,
and let him resume his task.

439
01:04:01.692 --> 01:04:06.276
You who lives and reigns
from everlasting to everlasting. Amen.

440
01:05:24.242 --> 01:05:26.201
You have a visitor.

441
01:05:41.159 --> 01:05:44.076
- What is it?
- I'm afraid.

442
01:05:46.367 --> 01:05:49.826
I can not stand being alone in that room.

443
01:05:55.117 --> 01:05:58.159
Now you get the Chancellor
to follow you up the room.

444
01:05:58.326 --> 01:06:00.742
Now I'll look after you.

445
01:08:05.667 --> 01:08:07.542
Inge.

446
01:08:11.001 --> 01:08:13.584
Come on. Come on.

447
01:08:17.292 --> 01:08:20.001
Gisle! Let me out!

448
01:08:22.042 --> 01:08:24.001
- No!
- Gisle!

449
01:08:28.292 --> 01:08:30.709
Hey.

450
01:08:30.876 --> 01:08:34.667
Welcome to the farm! Hello.

451
01:08:41.792 --> 01:08:44.292
Welcome to the farm.

452
01:08:54.751 --> 01:08:58.167
- We must continue. We must continue.
- Torstein. Torstein.

453
01:08:58.334 --> 01:09:01.292
Relax. Calm down.

454
01:09:01.459 --> 01:09:04.001
- Where's Haakon?
- He is asleep.

455
01:09:09.001 --> 01:09:10.834
Torstein.

456
01:09:14.001 --> 01:09:16.042
I'm here.

457
01:09:35.334 --> 01:09:37.459
Drink this.

458
01:09:41.084 --> 01:09:42.876
More.

459
01:09:44.084 --> 01:09:46.167
- What is it?
- Fish oil.

460
01:09:46.334 --> 01:09:50.001
- You need nourishment, Torstein.
- Yes, yes, yes.

461
01:09:57.917 --> 01:10:00.126
Then it's your turn.

462
01:10:16.709 --> 01:10:19.376
- Can I have some more?
- You want some more?

463
01:10:19.542 --> 01:10:21.459
Thank you.

464
01:10:47.917 --> 01:10:51.292
- What is this?
- You think people go willingly to war?

465
01:10:51.459 --> 01:10:54.917
- So you invited to blot?
- Yes.

466
01:10:56.626 --> 01:10:59.542
- Do they know they are going to war?
- No.

467
01:11:02.501 --> 01:11:06.292
- And it was all you could get?
- Yes.

468
01:11:06.459 --> 01:11:10.167
This is not working.
They do not know that they are going to war.

469
01:11:12.626 --> 01:11:14.584
Shut up!

470
01:11:15.042 --> 01:11:16.751
Listen!

471
01:11:16.917 --> 01:11:20.459
We have Birkebeiner in the house!

472
01:11:25.167 --> 01:11:28.126
I'm not Birkebeiner.

473
01:11:28.292 --> 01:11:32.001
I'm just like you.
I am a poor farmer.

474
01:11:32.126 --> 01:11:34.876
I try to cultivate the rock pile
we call land, -

475
01:11:35.042 --> 01:11:38.792
- And pray to God that the family
will get through the winter.

476
01:11:39.001 --> 01:11:43.334
Birkebeiners are the King's men.
But have they met him?

477
01:11:43.501 --> 01:11:47.792
He that hides in Nidaros while
Baglers burn down our country.

478
01:11:48.001 --> 01:11:52.667
He who sits on a golden chair, sleeping
in a silk bed and sucks his thumb.

479
01:11:55.084 --> 01:11:59.667
We are farmers, not warriors.
But we fight for what we love.

480
01:12:00.501 --> 01:12:04.126
For our families.
For them to survive.

481
01:12:09.001 --> 01:12:11.251
Baglers killed my wife.

482
01:12:12.584 --> 01:12:15.626
They killed my boy. Eirik.

483
01:12:17.834 --> 01:12:21.001
He was not even two years old.

484
01:12:23.209 --> 01:12:25.167
And for what?

485
01:12:28.001 --> 01:12:29.876
For what?

486
01:12:32.751 --> 01:12:37.376
The King in Nidaros is dead.
But Norway has a new King.

487
01:12:39.292 --> 01:12:42.417
And he is here today.

488
01:13:01.917 --> 01:13:05.292
This is the new King.
Haakon Haakonsson.

489
01:13:06.917 --> 01:13:10.417
It is he the Baglers is coming to kill.

490
01:13:11.209 --> 01:13:13.709
Help me stop the Baglers -

491
01:13:13.876 --> 01:13:17.376
- So we can gather us
under this King, -

492
01:13:20.126 --> 01:13:23.917
- And send these fuckers
back to hell.

493
01:13:25.584 --> 01:13:28.584
Help me. Help us.

494
01:13:31.292 --> 01:13:37.167
Not as farmers , but as this
King's men. Genuine Birkebeiner.

495
01:13:56.417 --> 01:13:58.751
Our new King.

496
01:14:11.209 --> 01:14:13.751
- Here, Frikk.
- No, I don't need one.

497
01:14:13.917 --> 01:14:16.917
- What?
- I'll take one of the Baglers.

498
01:14:50.167 --> 01:14:52.667
There is only one road through the valley.

499
01:14:52.834 --> 01:14:56.292
The King's son and Inga have to go first,
and they continue through the valley here.

500
01:14:56.584 --> 01:14:59.084
Audun is here, and I'm here.

501
01:14:59.251 --> 01:15:03.626
Here are the archers. Then Torstein leads
the Baglers through here.

502
01:15:03.792 --> 01:15:06.542
When they have come far enough,
the archers start shooting.

503
01:15:06.709 --> 01:15:08.459
- They're coming!
- What?

504
01:15:08.626 --> 01:15:10.917
There comes an army from the south.

505
01:15:11.084 --> 01:15:14.167
- It's the Baglers.
- All get ready!

506
01:15:14.334 --> 01:15:17.209
Come on! All together!

507
01:15:18.376 --> 01:15:20.084
Haakon?

508
01:15:20.792 --> 01:15:24.292
- Where's Haakon?
- Inga! Haakon is in the sled.

509
01:15:26.001 --> 01:15:29.501
- Audun, you know what to do?
- Yes.

510
01:15:30.834 --> 01:15:34.126
If they come through,
the boy dies.

511
01:15:34.292 --> 01:15:37.001
It will be okay. Trust me.

512
01:15:59.417 --> 01:16:03.876
So, so, it's okay, Haakon. Mom is here.
Mommy will watch over you.

513
01:16:04.584 --> 01:16:06.876
Quiet now, my dear.

514
01:16:10.084 --> 01:16:11.792
They are coming!

515
01:16:30.042 --> 01:16:31.667
Wait.

516
01:16:34.459 --> 01:16:36.001
Now!

517
01:16:50.301 --> 01:16:52.884
A little further. A little further.

518
01:16:55.634 --> 01:16:59.759
Wait here. Wait here.

519
01:17:02.967 --> 01:17:05.051
Wait.

520
01:17:31.967 --> 01:17:34.217
Now they are through.

521
01:17:35.509 --> 01:17:37.217
Wait.

522
01:17:42.426 --> 01:17:47.717
Now we are safe.
So, so. Now we are safe.

523
01:17:55.176 --> 01:17:57.676
Now they come. Stay, stay.

524
01:18:10.759 --> 01:18:12.342
Attack!

525
01:18:19.634 --> 01:18:23.592
Get off the horses! Attack, dammit!

526
01:19:28.809 --> 01:19:31.017
Skjervald!

527
01:19:42.184 --> 01:19:44.059
Here. Drink.

528
01:19:46.101 --> 01:19:49.059
Welcome to Ragnarok!

529
01:19:51.517 --> 01:19:54.059
They came through!
Stop the horses!

530
01:19:58.767 --> 01:20:01.101
Skjervald, come on!

531
01:20:02.851 --> 01:20:05.101
We'll catch up to them.

532
01:20:10.392 --> 01:20:12.392
What did you say?

533
01:20:13.934 --> 01:20:16.851
Skjervald!
Hang on! We are going!

534
01:20:37.851 --> 01:20:42.351
Egil! Calm. We're through.
Now it's up to Skjervald.

535
01:20:47.726 --> 01:20:53.309
- They came through, dammit!
- Go! Egil, come on!

536
01:21:39.142 --> 01:21:41.642
It's just loose horses.

537
01:22:08.142 --> 01:22:09.517
Come on, faster!

538
01:22:13.226 --> 01:22:15.934
They are right behind us. Come on!

539
01:22:29.642 --> 01:22:33.351
Come on! Faster, Egil!

540
01:22:33.517 --> 01:22:35.684
Continue! We will stop them.

541
01:23:09.142 --> 01:23:11.434
Skjervald! He came through!

542
01:23:48.059 --> 01:23:49.976
Traitor!

543
01:23:56.142 --> 01:23:59.226
For God's sake, Egil, faster!

544
01:24:00.392 --> 01:24:02.642
Faster!

545
01:24:29.476 --> 01:24:32.976
Please! He's just a child.
Let him go.

546
01:25:14.184 --> 01:25:17.184
Egil! Get up! We must go!

547
01:25:50.684 --> 01:25:52.684
Skjervald.

548
01:25:54.017 --> 01:25:55.767
Skjervald!

549
01:26:19.226 --> 01:26:21.767
Skjervald. Skjervald.

550
01:26:25.642 --> 01:26:28.476
You did it. You made it.

551
01:26:32.517 --> 01:26:35.059
We will all die.

552
01:26:35.226 --> 01:26:38.601
But our legacy lives on.

553
01:28:06.484 --> 01:28:09.192
That's fine. Away, away.

554
01:28:11.984 --> 01:28:15.609
It's okay.
There will be no wedding.

555
01:28:15.776 --> 01:28:19.026
But do not show that you are afraid, Christina.

556
01:28:23.942 --> 01:28:28.317
There are some who have started rebelling
and have surrounded Nidaros Cathedral.

557
01:28:30.901 --> 01:28:36.401
So, we will be holding the
wedding here at the palace.

558
01:28:37.442 --> 01:28:40.359
We're getting married here. No guests.

559
01:28:41.901 --> 01:28:44.651
Do you know anything about this?

560
01:28:44.817 --> 01:28:46.984
- No.
- Come here.

561
01:28:49.442 --> 01:28:51.442
I know nothing.

562
01:29:44.109 --> 01:29:46.151
Birkebeiners.

563
01:29:47.484 --> 01:29:50.109
I have to talk to Inge.

564
01:29:50.276 --> 01:29:53.401
Let me talk to Inge Baardsson. Now.

565
01:29:56.067 --> 01:30:01.567
Wait! This is Haakon Haakonsson.
He is Norway's rightful King.

566
01:30:16.442 --> 01:30:18.776
No! Let me go!

567
01:30:22.192 --> 01:30:26.526
He is the King's son!
I swear by the boy's life!

568
01:30:32.776 --> 01:30:36.359
In the absence of your father, King Sverre, -

569
01:30:36.526 --> 01:30:40.609
- I give you,
Christina Sverresdatter, -

570
01:30:42.276 --> 01:30:49.192
-to Earl Gisle, to honor and
to be his wife, to half bed and half property.

571
01:31:05.026 --> 01:31:07.442
Now I know who you are.

572
01:31:45.276 --> 01:31:49.776
It was God's will that you and
Skjervald would rescue the King's son.

573
01:31:50.776 --> 01:31:55.151
Therefore I appoint you to Haakon
Haakonssons protector.

574
01:31:57.276 --> 01:32:00.442
With Birkebeiners consent
I shall guard the throne -

575
01:32:00.609 --> 01:32:04.442
-to Haakon becomes old enough
to govern himself.

576
01:32:10.184 --> 01:32:13.184
You shall bring peace to our country.
